{
  "info": {
    "name": "Stock Portfolio Backend",
    "description": "All 11 endpoints of the stock_portfolio_be server (Express 5 + Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL).\n\n**How to use**\n1. Set `baseUrl` in the collection variables (default `http://localhost:5001`).\n2. Run **Auth → Register** or **Auth → Login**. The test script saves the JWT into the `token` variable, and every other request sends it as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` automatically.\n3. Run **Broker accounts → Link broker account**. The test script saves `brokerAccountId` and `portfolioId` for the requests that need them.\n4. Run **Sync trades** within 15 minutes of linking (the broker session lives in memory and expires).\n\nFull documentation: `docs/API_DOCUMENTATION.md`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5001", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "brokerAccountId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "portfolioId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "ali@example.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "secret123", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "brokerAccountNumber", "value": "CC12345", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "brokerPassword", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "No token needed. Both requests return a JWT that the test script stores in `{{token}}`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Ali Khan\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a user and returns a login token.\n\n**Responses**\n- `201` `{ message: \"success\", data: { id, fullName }, token }`\n- `400` `{ message: \"user already exists\" }`\n- `500` HTML page if a required field is missing (no validation yet)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', json.token);",
                  "  console.log('token saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "201 Created",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ali@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Ali Khan\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] }
              },
              "status": "Created",
              "code": 201,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": { \"id\": \"3f1c…\", \"fullName\": \"Ali Khan\" },\n  \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOi…\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "400 user already exists",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ali@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\",\n  \"fullName\": \"Ali Khan\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] }
              },
              "status": "Bad Request",
              "code": 400,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{ \"message\": \"user already exists\" }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in and returns a JWT (valid 7 days by default).\n\n**Responses**\n- `200` `{ status: \"success\", data: { user: { id, fullName, email }, token } }`\n- `401` `{ message: \"Invalid email or passowrd\" }` — same message for unknown email and wrong password."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json?.data?.token;",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', token);",
                  "  console.log('token saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ali@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"user\": { \"id\": \"3f1c…\", \"fullName\": \"Ali Khan\", \"email\": \"ali@example.com\" },\n    \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOi…\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Invalid credentials",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"ali@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{ \"message\": \"Invalid email or passowrd\" }"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Broker accounts",
      "description": "Needs `{{token}}`. Link an AHL eTrade account, list, disconnect, and sync trades.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Link broker account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumber\": \"{{brokerAccountNumber}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{brokerPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["broker", "accounts"]
            },
            "description": "Logs in to the AHL eTrade website with the broker credentials, creates (or re-activates) the `broker_accounts` row and its portfolio (`AHL <accountNumber>`), and keeps the broker cookies in server memory for **15 minutes**. The broker password is never stored.\n\nThe test script saves `brokerAccountId` and `portfolioId` into collection variables.\n\n**Responses**\n- `200` `{ data: { brokerAccountId, portfolioId, status, sessionCookie, cookies, enabledDigits } }`\n- `400` `{ error: \"accountNumber and password are required.\" }`\n- `400` `{ error: \"Password is too short: the broker asked for character N.\" }`\n- `401` `{ error: \"Invalid broker credentials.\" }`\n- `502` `{ error: \"No session cookie was returned by the broker login page.\" }`\n- `502` `{ error: \"No enabled Digit fields were found in the broker login page.\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json?.data?.brokerAccountId) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('brokerAccountId', json.data.brokerAccountId);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('portfolioId', json.data.portfolioId);",
                  "  console.log('brokerAccountId + portfolioId saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumber\": \"CC12345\",\n  \"password\": \"MyBrokerPass1\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"brokerAccountId\": \"8a2e…\",\n    \"portfolioId\": \"c47b…\",\n    \"status\": 302,\n    \"sessionCookie\": \".AspNetCore.Session=CfDJ8…\",\n    \"cookies\": { \".AspNetCore.Session\": \"CfDJ8…\", \"trader\": \"CC12345\", \"HouseName\": \"AHL\" },\n    \"enabledDigits\": [1, 4, 7]\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Invalid broker credentials",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"accountNumber\": \"CC12345\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong\"\n}" },
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts"] }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{ \"error\": \"Invalid broker credentials.\" }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List broker accounts",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["broker", "accounts"]
            },
            "description": "Lists the caller's linked broker accounts, newest first, each with its portfolio.\n\n`syncStatus` is `idle` or `disconnected`; `lastSyncedAt` is `null` until the first sync.\n\nIf `brokerAccountId` / `portfolioId` are still empty, the test script fills them from the first account."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const accounts = pm.response.json()?.data?.accounts ?? [];",
                  "pm.test('accounts is an array', () => pm.expect(accounts).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "const first = accounts[0];",
                  "if (first && !pm.collectionVariables.get('brokerAccountId')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('brokerAccountId', first.id);",
                  "  if (first.portfolios?.[0]?.id) pm.collectionVariables.set('portfolioId', first.portfolios[0].id);",
                  "  console.log('brokerAccountId + portfolioId filled from first account');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"accounts\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"8a2e…\",\n        \"broker\": \"AHL_ETRADE\",\n        \"clientCode\": \"CC12345\",\n        \"syncStatus\": \"idle\",\n        \"lastSyncedAt\": \"2026-09-04T09:15:22.000Z\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-30T12:00:00.000Z\",\n        \"portfolios\": [ { \"id\": \"c47b…\", \"name\": \"AHL CC12345\" } ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sync trades",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts/{{brokerAccountId}}/sync",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["broker", "accounts", "{{brokerAccountId}}", "sync"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "from", "value": "2022-01-01", "description": "Start date YYYY-MM-DD (default 2022-01-01)", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "to", "value": "2026-09-04", "description": "End date YYYY-MM-DD (default today)", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "type", "value": "ALL", "description": "Passed to the broker: BUY, SELL or ALL (default ALL)", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "scrip", "value": "ALL", "description": "Passed to the broker: one symbol or ALL (default ALL)", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Downloads the broker's order history and current holdings, upserts securities and trades, recomputes positions (average-cost method, merged with the broker's holdings) and records today's price for each held stock.\n\nDoes **not** log in — it reuses the in-memory session from *Link broker account*. Run it within 15 minutes of linking, otherwise you get `401` and must link again. Safe to re-run: trades are not duplicated.\n\nAll query params are optional; enable them in the Params tab to override the defaults.\n\n**Responses**\n- `200` `{ message: \"success\", data: { securities, trades, positions, prices, fromCollaterals, fromTrades, mismatches[], from, to } }`\n- `401` `{ error: \"Broker session expired. Reconnect the account to continue.\" }`\n- `404` `{ error: \"account does not exist\" }`"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const data = pm.response.json()?.data;",
                  "if (data) console.log(`trades: ${data.trades}, positions: ${data.positions}, mismatches: ${data.mismatches?.length ?? 0}`);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts/{{brokerAccountId}}/sync", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts", "{{brokerAccountId}}", "sync"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"securities\": 12,\n    \"trades\": 87,\n    \"positions\": 9,\n    \"prices\": 7,\n    \"fromCollaterals\": 7,\n    \"fromTrades\": 2,\n    \"mismatches\": [\n      {\n        \"symbol\": \"FFC\",\n        \"computedQty\": 500,\n        \"brokerQty\": 550,\n        \"delta\": 50,\n        \"impliedRatio\": 1.1,\n        \"costBasisMatches\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"from\": \"2022-01-01\",\n    \"to\": \"2026-09-04\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            {
              "name": "401 Broker session expired",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts/{{brokerAccountId}}/sync", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts", "{{brokerAccountId}}", "sync"] }
              },
              "status": "Unauthorized",
              "code": 401,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{ \"error\": \"Broker session expired. Reconnect the account to continue.\" }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Disconnect broker account",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts/{{brokerAccountId}}/disconnect",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["broker", "accounts", "{{brokerAccountId}}", "disconnect"]
            },
            "description": "Unlinks the broker account: sets `syncStatus` to `disconnected`. Trades, positions and the portfolio are **kept**.\n\n**Responses**\n- `200` `{ message: \"account disconnected successfully\", data: { account: { id, clientCode, syncStatus } } }`\n- `404` `{ error: \"account does not exist\" }` — not found or belongs to another user."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('syncStatus is disconnected', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()?.data?.account?.syncStatus).to.eql('disconnected'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "PATCH",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/broker/accounts/{{brokerAccountId}}/disconnect", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["broker", "accounts", "{{brokerAccountId}}", "disconnect"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"account disconnected successfully\",\n  \"data\": { \"account\": { \"id\": \"8a2e…\", \"clientCode\": \"CC12345\", \"syncStatus\": \"disconnected\" } }\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Portfolio",
      "description": "Needs `{{token}}`. Read-only views of the portfolio built by the sync.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List portfolios",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/portfolio/getPortfolioList",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["portfolio", "getPortfolioList"]
            },
            "description": "Lists the caller's portfolios. One portfolio is created automatically per linked broker account, named `AHL <clientCode>`, base currency `PKR`.\n\nIf `portfolioId` is still empty, the test script fills it from the first portfolio."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const list = pm.response.json()?.data?.portfoliolist ?? [];",
                  "if (list[0] && !pm.collectionVariables.get('portfolioId')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('portfolioId', list[0].id);",
                  "  console.log('portfolioId filled from first portfolio');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/portfolio/getPortfolioList", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["portfolio", "getPortfolioList"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"success\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"portfoliolist\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"c47b…\",\n        \"userId\": \"3f1c…\",\n        \"brokerAccountId\": \"8a2e…\",\n        \"name\": \"AHL CC12345\",\n        \"baseCurrency\": \"PKR\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-30T12:00:00.000Z\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Positions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/portfolio/{{portfolioId}}/positions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["portfolio", "{{portfolioId}}", "positions"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "from", "value": "2025-09-05", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD — enable together with `to` to get a `trend` array per position", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "to", "value": "2026-09-05", "description": "YYYY-MM-DD — inclusive; window max 5 years", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Current holdings with the latest known price and P&L, plus a summary. All numbers are real JSON numbers.\n\n- `lastPrice` / `marketValue` / `unrealizedPnl` are `null` when no price is stored yet for that stock.\n- `summary` totals cover **only priced positions**; `unpricedPositions` says how many were left out.\n- A portfolio that is not yours returns an empty `positions` array (200, not 404).\n\n**Trend:** every position carries `trend: [ { date, close }, … ]` (oldest first) for the window in `data.range`. The default window is the last 12 months ending today; enable both `from` and `to` in the Params tab to change it. A stock with no bars in the window gets `trend: []` but keeps its `lastPrice`.\n\n**Which stocks:** only those held at some point inside the window (quantity above zero at `from`, or a BUY inside it). A stock bought after `to`, or fully sold before `from`, is left out; `summary` totals only the rows returned.\n\n**400** when only one date is sent, a date is not `YYYY-MM-DD`, `from` is after `to`, or the window is wider than 5 years."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const data = pm.response.json()?.data;",
                  "pm.test('has positions and summary', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(data?.positions).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(data?.summary).to.be.an('object');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 OK",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/portfolio/{{portfolioId}}/positions", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["portfolio", "{{portfolioId}}", "positions"] }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json; charset=utf-8" }],
